---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { productUrl } from '../lib/site-links';
import '../styles/editorial.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Hyphos Inc. is Daniel Newton's consulting and software company. We connect systems and knowledge around the way people work.">
<section class="editorial-hero page-shell"><p class="section-label">About Hyphos Inc.</p><h1>Good systems give<br />people room.</h1><p>Room to think. To care for customers. To do the part of the work that depends on their experience and judgment.</p></section>
<section class="editorial-body page-shell"><div class="editorial-aside"><span class="section-label">The person behind the work</span><h2>Daniel Newton</h2><p>Consulting & software<br />Hyphos Inc.</p><a href="/contact" class="text-link">Start a conversation ↗</a></div><div class="editorial-prose"><h2>Start with what people actually do.</h2><p>The work rarely fits neatly into the software. Someone keeps a spreadsheet on the side. Someone remembers the exception. Someone knows who to call.</p><p>Hyphos starts there. We look at how the business runs, connect the information it depends on, and build software around the work.</p><h2>Stay close enough to build the right thing.</h2><p>You work directly with Daniel. We talk with the people using the systems, make the problem concrete, and show working software early.</p><p>Some problems need an integration. Some need custom software. Some need a clearer process. The useful answer starts with understanding which one you're facing.</p><h2>Two ways to work with Hyphos.</h2><p>Our consulting work helps businesses connect operations and build tools that fit. The <a href={productUrl}>Hyphos product</a> focuses on the knowledge behind the work: decisions, experience and context that a team can use again.</p><p>They share the same premise. The systems should carry more of the coordination, so people can give more attention to the work that needs them.</p><a href="/work" class="text-link">See the work ↗</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
